From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:31:40 +0000
Subject: build: give rust_macro steps their own pool

Proc-macro crates are rustc compiles that produce a shared library, and
the rust_macro tool puts them in build_toolchain_link_pool, whose depth is
concurrent_links (2 by default on Linux). A build has about 20 of them at
5-12s each, all ready early, so for the first ~100s of a build they hold
both link pool slots while the links of host tools on the critical path
(brotli, flatc, torque, mksnapshot, ...) queue for 17-75s.

Give rust_macro its own pool of the same depth, so proc-macro builds no
longer block those links. In local measurements this took the number of
links that waited more than 5s for the pool from 22 to 0-1, and the
longest wait from 58s to 3-7s.

This should be upstreamed. Drop this patch once upstream
build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni no longer puts the rust_macro tool in
link_pool; check that line on each Chromium roll.

diff --git a/build/toolchain/BUILD.gn b/build/toolchain/BUILD.gn
index 6f3bc67d1fa38724f7c475a1160c1e9c7814a53a..8fa1b59b0e5ae693028943e83b31b2fd35fca20f 100644
--- a/build/toolchain/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/toolchain/BUILD.gn
@@ -19,6 +19,13 @@ if (current_toolchain == default_toolchain) {
     depth = concurrent_links
   }
 
+  # Proc-macro crates are rustc compiles that produce a shared library.
+  # Give them their own pool, so they don't hold link_pool slots needed
+  # by the links of host tools that are on the critical path.
+  pool("rust_macro_pool") {
+    depth = concurrent_links
+  }
+
   pool("action_pool") {
     depth = action_pool_depth
   }
diff --git a/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni b/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni
index 747bb03f96703868ccf6db92ea1fb01d16867a7a..4910842f48a4131402e2eb26492011747582d090 100644
--- a/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni
+++ b/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni
@@ -868,7 +868,7 @@ template("single_gcc_toolchain") {
         dllname = "{{output_dir}}/{{target_output_name}}{{output_extension}}"
         depfile = "$dllname.d"
         rspfile = rustc_rsp_path
-        pool = "//build/toolchain:link_pool($default_toolchain)"
+        pool = "//build/toolchain:rust_macro_pool($default_toolchain)"
 
         default_output_extension = default_shlib_extension
         output_prefix = "lib"
